ved into the game yes they  can take  this knight if they want to but if they  do  they will be able to attack an isolated  pawn here uh but also white now has the  bishop pair  and so uh both sides equal in material  but  in an open board state like this i'm  definitely taking the bishop pair  um from white i think that's going to be  the the better option  going into the middle and end game  the last variation we're going to look  at is if they play pawn to b5 they may  not know what you're doing if you play  knight to a4  kind of looks like you're a crazy person  so they could just start throwing all  their material trying to  see how they can get you in a tough  position pawn to b5 but knight to c5  is a great little outpost they have no  pawns that can ever  force this knight to move and so how do  they really respond here well they could  play bishop 2 g7  the main themes that they are used to  playing  you're going to continue with this same  thing that you're used to playing and  that is e4  attacking this knight right here maybe  knight comes back here to  b6 and then i recommend knight to f3  yes you could play bishop to b5  check the problem is they can play c6  pretty easily  the bishop comes back and then you're in  a tough spot because queen takes on  d4 if you take it  yes their bishop recaptures but you can  see you've lost  control of the center of the board  they're attacking your knight here on c5  this is not a position that's going to  go favorably for white so instead  while it does look tempting and you can  take this at some point  i recommend first playing knight to f3  you really want to control  this pawn here on a d4 now they have a  couple options one  they could let you take this pawn here  on b5 which isn't great or they could  start to play something like a6 but this  is  not really when you start to think about  all  the the moves that they want to be  playing in the groomfell defense this is  not how they want to do it  protecting their pawn here on b5 with a6  this is just letting you control the  center of the board they really want to  be building around  this bishop on g7 and getting their  other pieces to attack this year on the  board if they're playing a6  that feels like a very big win  for you now we come back maybe they  don't play bishop to g7  maybe they play something else who knows  really what they could play in this  position knight two  d7 maybe you're still pushing forward  with  e4 here maybe if they take  you take with your own pawn here on uh  c5 maybe they play b4 things get  crazy now bishop takes on  b5 check maybe they play c6  you could play a3 just say hey if you  want to take my queen that's fine we  could have an exchange on the board  white's gonna be up in material yes they  have double pawns on the b  file uh but supporting this pass pawn  right here  on the c file you have a semi-open file  that your rook can get involved into the  game  it's just very difficult to see how  they're going to  respond so yeah if you see that pawn to  b5 definitely wouldn't be too worried  after knight to c5 you're going to be in  a  pretty good spot hopefully you enjoyed  this video on a creative way to  attack the greenfield defense it's a  very common defense from black so you  get a lot of opportunity to play it  but this is one that i fancy myself so  let me know what your favorite defense  against the grunfeld defense is or if  you've tried this out and you've had  success let me know  if there's other variations that you  want to see feel free to let me know in  the comments you can always reach me  on my website thejustwebsite.com you can  always reach out to me via email  the chess website at gmail.com but thank  you so much for watching the video if  you haven't already  hit the like button make sure you are  subscribed so you can make sure  that you are notified anytime i make  more videos but thanks so much and i'll  see you in the next video
 

